																		Author Commentary: Conspiracy, Epilogue
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/hornby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1259135); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1259135&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609882012" alt="Hornby" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1259135)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/hornby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1259135); return false;" >Hornby</a></span> <span class="odate time_1344882367 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Aug 2012 18:26</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1536125">
									

<p>This is the Epilogue of <em>Conspiracy</em>. It is not so much a horror story as an intrigue thriller. I have studied intelligence and espionage fairly extensively throughout university, writing my senior thesis on intelligence analysis. This tale is essentially an attempt to write up a good spy story in the world of the SCP Foundation.</p>
<p>I hope you have enjoyed <em>Conspiracy</em>; thanks for reading!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Commentary&nbsp;involving&nbsp;spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">hide&nbsp;spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>Tim Harper as O5-7 has appeared in multiple other tales, including (to date) <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/project-heimdall-prologue">the Project Heimdall prologue</a> and <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/neptune-station">Neptune Station</a>.</li>
<li>O5-1 does not mention recovering the liquid provided as payment to Sir James. This supports the conclusion that the Foundation decided recovering a sample of anomalous liquid from a slow but renewable source (SCP-006 being a <em>spring</em>, however small) was less important than keeping on good terms with a well-connected information broker willing to do business with the Foundation. After all, a grateful ally is more valuable than an angry and dangerous adversary. It is also possible it was simply not a topic for discussion at the time, and the Foundation did intend to recover the liquid. Either decision would likely have required discussion of the O5 Council, and thus would have likely had both those in favor of a recovery attempt, and those opposed.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<div class="collapsible-block">
