		<div class="post" id="post-1536309">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,1536309)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-1536309">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sregan" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1386518); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1386518&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609882012" alt="SRegan" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1386518)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sregan" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1386518); return false;" >SRegan</a></span> <span class="odate time_1344895676 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Aug 2012 22:07</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1536309">
									

<p>Congratulations - first of all on the epic length and coherence of the series. It highlighted some SCPs I hadn't come across before, including 557, and did a spectacular job in tying them all together into a plausible world.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The snowballing effect of the fake conspiracy was done exceedingly well, especially the Foundation's own tendency to read unconnected events into what they consider to be an unfolding plot, such as the death of O5-11. As I mentioned in my comment on Part VII I was slightly perturbed by the implication that fairly junior Russian army officers are privy to at least some knowledge of the Foundation, though on reflection he doesn't display great knowledge of what's going on behind the Veil. For some reason I also had the notion that during the Cold War the Foundation was more or less denied access to the Eastern Bloc, with groups like GRU Division &quot;P&quot; taking their role in the Soviet Union, though perhaps I've been oversimplifying matters.</p>
</div>
</div>
